        "id": 1792208205,
        "content": "- There's some commands, apparently `allow` and `wallet` that are too loose for parsing. \r\n- The only time a command should be parsed is if a comment begins with `/` and the entire body of the comment is only used for the command. \r\n- I can't think of a single instance where a user wanted to invoke a bot command inside of a normal comment, so this should not be possible at all. \r\n_Originally posted by @ubiquibot[bot] in https://github.com/ubiquity/ubiquibot/issues/464#issuecomment-1624284734_",
